    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, serving as our highest-value assets. **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) is the primary engine against Elmer Rodr\u00edguez; the combination of a favorable 5.31 xERA matchup and the premium #3 spot maximizes his run-production potential. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (77.88) benefits from facing the vulnerable Seymour, and despite a slight park penalty, his elite profile makes him a must-start. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also projects as a strong play, as the favorable 4.41 xERA of Shane Baz creates a prime environment for him to deliver high-efficiency returns in the middle of our order.\n\nBeyond our top-tier producers, **Andy Pages** (63.30) and **Heliot Ramos** (62.61) represent our most interesting mid-tier contributors. **Andy Pages** gets a significant boost from the targetable Seymour, while **Heliot Ramos** relies on his assumed #3 slotting to pad his score despite a neutral platoon stance. The decision to bench secondary options like **Jacob Wilson** or **Drake Baldwin** came down to a lack of elite sprint speed or lineup volatility; as SB remains our scarcest category, **Nasim Nunez** (48.96) holds his position despite a low order placement because his specific skill set fits our roster construction goals. \n\nWe are monitoring several lineup-pending situations, specifically for **Coby Mayo**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Gunnar Henderson**. If any of these players are shuffled down the order, their efficiency scores will adjust downward accordingly. While **Liam Hicks** (42.84) and **Wade Meckler** (42.21) sit near the floor of our utility threshold, we are maintaining them in the starting lineup to capitalize on the volume of plate appearances, provided they survive the risks posed by pitchers like Wheeler and Gilbert. We remain disciplined in holding **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, keeping our eyes locked on our remaining active roster to close the gap in Roto standings.",
